---
// The small mark before the site name in the top bar: a Swiss cross in the accent. Decorative:
// it sits inside the home link, whose name is the tagline, so it is hidden from assistive tech.
// The cross is accent-text on paper and accent-bright on the dark bar. Its arms are a sixth
// longer than they are wide, as on the Swiss flag.
---

<svg class="site-mark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <path d="M9 2h6v7h7v6h-7v7H9v-7H2V9h7z" />
</svg>

<style>
  /* The name hangs beside the mark when it wraps on a phone. */
  :global(*:has(> .site-mark)) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .site-mark {
    flex: none;
    width: 1.25rem;
    height: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.125rem; /* centred on the first 1.5rem line */
    fill: var(--accent-text);
  }
  :global(html[data-menu='open']) .site-mark,
  :global(html[data-drawer-open]) .site-mark {
    fill: var(--accent-bright);
  }
</style>
